Z||000011||turbo86se||12-05-2000||12:03 PM||||Black88GT, yes my 2.8 is completely stock. I've only done modifications to the exhaust, such as ported and polished manifolds, coated inside and out with Jet Hot's ceramic coating, removed the cat.convertor, K&N air filter, polyurethane dog bone. <BR>Hey, I'll be in Frederick, MD around x-mas time, I'll email you. Too bad I won't be driving the Fiero. 10 days worth of clothes and a 3 year-old german shepard don't fit!! LOL<P>Red, you can email me at turbo86se@webtv.net<BR>I'll have to check out what you're asking about, keep in mind I have no mechanical abilities whatsoever (is that one word?)!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Hartz||12-05-2000||07:41 PM||||Here's the list of stuff I did to the engine when I placed the turbo on it:<P>Parts:<P>ARP Head and Main studs, washers, nuts, rod bolts, and nuts.<BR>Accel 8.8 Spiral Core plug wires.<BR>MSD 6BTM Ignition (Boost Timing Master version of 6AL)<BR>Accel Super Coil<BR>JE Pistons, custom forged aluminum (8.57:1 CR), tool steel pins, locks, and rings.<BR>Crane Compucam and Lifters (P/N 254122)<BR>Crane Valve Springs (P/N 99848-12)<BR>Crane Retainers (P/N 99915-12)<BR>Crane Locks (P/N 99041-1)<BR>Valve Seals<BR>3.1 Liter Crankshaft (General Motors)<BR>Melling High Volume oil pump<BR>Air Research T-10 Turbocharger<BR>Fel Pro Gasket set with O-Ring Head Gasket.<BR>Rod, Main, and Cam Bearings<BR>AC R41-TS Spark Plugs<BR>Cloyes True Roller Timing set<BR>TH125-C Automatic Transmission shift kit<BR>Custom 2 1/2" mandral-bent exhaust system<BR>Supertrapp Stainless Steel 4A Muffer system (P/N 446-2010)<P>Machine Work:<P>Balance and Blueprint<BR>Crossdrill crank, straighten and polish.<BR>Valve job - full radius, hand lapped and blended<BR>Resurface Heads.<BR>Cut Decks<BR>Float Rods<BR>Bore and Hone with Deck Plate<BR>Port Cylinder Heads <BR>Port Match exhaust manifolds<BR>Port Match Intake Manifold and Runners<BR>Polish side beams on rods<BR>Fabricate custom air intake to replace stock air inlet.<P>Not the cheapest or easiest way to make power, in retrospect, but it's fun and I enjoy it.<P>Hartz<BR>'85 Fiero SE turbo V6<P>||||reg||7
