Z||000022||ArmandoP||12-07-2000||04:28 AM||||WOW!, now if only pontiac would have done that from the factory, my MR2 would not ahve stood a freaking chance!<BR>Im REALLY curious as to what the V6 turbo pulls in the quarter.  My guess is somewhere in the "holy cow" range.  to those of you who have done the mod yourslef, can I contact you somehow? Im am SERIOUSLY considering turboing my 87MR2, and Id like to gain some knowledge from you.  everybody I know, 2 of em, that has turboed a MKI MR2 is pulling like 16 or more lbs of boost and I dont quite need THAT much, so Id like to pick your brains if possible.<BR>my email is ajperez@indiana.edu<BR>AIM mandosax<BR>as far as stock mr2, yeah, youd probably dust it, drivers being equal....but remember, the turbo MR2 engine is the same engine thats in the pikes peak toyotas (rod milles and the celica)  with bolt ons that engine can produce in excess of 450hp an well over 350lb feet of tourque.  the engine in my car is a different story though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>nice engine though...lokks very well done!<BR>Armando<P>------------------<BR>__________________<BR>will work for MR2 parts!!! <BR>1987 MR2 NA t-bar csp with 700 miles on its new engine. <BR>TRD copper head gasket, milled head .020, 2 short shifters,metal masters rear brake pads, 195-60-14 (soon to get new tires), clear corners, Clevite 77 bearings, NO A/C, MAF relocation mod, red silicon vacuum hoses, redline tranny fluid,and the stock exhaust with a WHOLE bunch of broken welds! <BR>indiana/illinois MR2 owners club<BR>[URLhttp://php.indiana.edu/~ajperez/inimoc.html[/URL]<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://php.indiana.edu/~ajperez/mytwo.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000023||Predator||12-07-2000||10:26 AM||||Great 1FST2M6. I would love to get it dyno checked when it is done. I am hoping to get it done within the next week.I got one word of warning from Kevin from Design1Systems. I still have the stock clutch, and he said not to get into it to hard or I won't have my clutch any longer. I may have to see about swapping it out later, but I need to get the car running again for a while before I start that up. My wife has been patient about it being in the garage for a month as it is. I don't want to push it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
